// `unsafe` marks a CONTAINED region, and `main` contains the whole program — so an `unsafe fn main`
// switches off every containment rule the seam installs (raw-pointer acquisition, `addr(of:)`, the
// `extern fn` call gate) for the entire program at once, which is the marker meaning nothing at all.
//
// The positive counterpart is every other fixture in this suite: a kama `unsafe fn` is callable FROM
// safe code (only an `extern fn` is gated at the call), so the raw work moves one frame down and
// `main` stays safe. `tests/unsafe_ptr.kama` is the canonical shape.
unsafe fn int32 main() {
    int32 x = 42;
    return x;
}
